{{! Everything a page needs to install and run as an app, shared by the main
    and bare (sign-in, setup) layouts so the two can never drift.
    - manifest.json covers Android, ChromeOS and desktop installs.
    - iOS ignores the manifest's icons and splash: it needs apple-touch-icon,
      the apple-mobile-web-app-* tags, and one launch screen per device size
      (without one it opens on a blank white screen). Portrait only: the
      launch screens are the canvas color with the app tile in the middle.
    - viewport-fit=cover + the translucent status bar let pages run edge to
      edge; layouts pad with env(safe-area-inset-*) to stay clear of the notch.
    - theme-color follows the chosen theme so the status bar matches. }}
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="manifest" href="/manifest.json">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/icons/pickaxe-apple-touch.png">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#16191c">
<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="MSM">
<meta name="application-name" content="MSM">
<meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no">
